---
# The shape of a site vault, for reference only. Never encrypt this file, never
# use it by a run: the real file is `vault.yml` beside it, encrypted with
# `ansible-vault` and committed as ciphertext.
#
# Create it with:
#   cp group_vars/all/vault.yml.example group_vars/all/vault.yml
#   # replace every CHANGEME value
#   ansible-vault encrypt group_vars/all/vault.yml
#
# Run with `--ask-vault-pass` (or a password file outside this tree).
#
# Every name is prefixed `vault_` and is mapped onto the name a unit file reads
# in `group_vars/all/vars.yml`, so a unit declaration never names a `vault_`
# variable.
#
# The product itself needs no secret. A site that passes one to a unit keeps the
# real value here and the mapping in `group_vars/all/vars.yml`:
#
# vault_container_example_password: "CHANGEME"
